270 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 198 0 R
/E (I started by thinking about what I would need. I decided to use an ESP32, a microphone, a proximity sensor, lights and a buzzer. At that time, I did not even know what an ESP32 was or how a microphone could detect a notification sound. I also had no knowledge of coding or electronics. I had never worked with jumper wires before, and I did not know how different components connected to each other or how electricity went through them.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
271 0 obj
<<
