/T (Reflection on my Learning and Experience)
/E (Reflection on my Learning and Experience)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
389 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 221 0 R
/E (When I started this studio, I honestly had no idea how I was going to make something like this. I had never worked with electronics before. I did not even know what Arduino, ESP32 or Raspberry Pi were. The idea of working with wires, sensors and coding felt very difficult and confusing to me.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
390 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 221 0 R
/E (In the beginning, even understanding how one small component worked took a lot of time. Sometimes I would connect something and it would not work, and I would not even know what was wrong. I had to keep checking the wires, the code and the connections and try again.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
391 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 221 0 R
/E (There were many times when I felt frustrated. I realised that working with electronics needs a lot of patience. Things do not always work on the first try, and sometimes even a very small connection can stop the whole thing from working. I slowly learned to not get frustrated immediately and instead check what could be wrong and try again.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
392 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 221 0 R
/E (I learned that I do not have to know everything before I start. I started this project without knowing electronics, coding or 3D printing, but I learned these things while making the project. )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
393 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 221 0 R
/E (The biggest thing I am taking from this studio is the confidence that I can learn something that initially feels very new to me. At the beginning, I could not imagine myself making an electronic prototype. By the end of the studio, I had a tangible, working aftefact which made by me in front of me that I had built through all those small steps.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
394 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 221 0 R
/E (I am genuinely happy with what I made. More than just the final artefact, I am happy that I did not give up when the process became difficult. This studio taught me to be more patient, to keep trying when things fail, and to trust the process of learning by doing.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
395 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 221 0 R
/E (I started the studio not knowing about electronics and ended it with a working object made using electronics, coding and 3D printing. For me, that is probably the biggest learning from these seven weeks.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
