/Title (The studio began with an exploration of the Luddite Movement and its relationship with technology. During the Industrial Revolution, machines were introduced into textile production and started replacing the work of skilled workers. Many workers feared of losing their jobs and livelihoods because of these machines. In response, they destroyed machines as a form of protest.)
