860 0 obj
<<
/Title (This felt different from the other ideas because I could clearly observe it happening around me. I started paying attention to what happens in that small moment: I am doing something, the phone gives me a notification, I notice it, and my attention moves towards the phone.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 856 0 R
/Next 862 0 R
>>
endobj
861 0 obj
<<
/Title (DUMMY FORM)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 863 0 R
/Next 857 0 R
>>
endobj
862 0 obj
<<
/Title (I became interested in this shift of attention rather than the larger idea of phone usage. I was not trying to say that phones are bad or that people should stop using them. I wanted to understand this small everyday behaviour and what happens when a notification pulls us away from what we were already doing.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 860 0 R
/Next 864 0 R
>>
endobj
863 0 obj
<<
/Title (FINAL FORM - MOBILE STAND)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 865 0 R
/Next 861 0 R
>>
endobj
864 0 obj
<<
/Title (This became the direction I decided to take forward. I chose to focus on the protocol of notification and attention shift, which eventually led me towards the concept of Distraction Hook.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 862 0 R
/Next 866 0 R
>>
endobj
